```
[ nan  nan 8.56 8.66 8.3  7.72 7.38 7.24 7.68 8.04 8.36 8.42 8.34 7.98
 7.74 7.72 7.66 7.76 7.92 8.12 8.34 8.4   nan  nan]
```


:::
:::


### SAS

```sas
/* PROC EXPAND (SAS/ETS): cmovave = centred moving average */
proc expand data=auto out=auto_mm method=none;
  id Anno;
  convert Vendite = mm3 / transformout=(cmovave 3 trimleft 1 trimright 1);
  convert Vendite = mm5 / transformout=(cmovave 5 trimleft 2 trimright 2);
  convert Vendite = mm9 / transformout=(cmovave 9 trimleft 4 trimright 4);
run;
proc print data=auto_mm noobs; format mm3 mm5 8.2; run;
```
:::

The corresponding plot (Figure 4.2) is obtained with the following commands. The solid line shows G.M. car sales and the dashed lines the 3- and 5-term moving averages (respectively the longer and the shorter in the plot).

::: {.panel-tabset group="language"}
### R


::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
plot(Vendite, main="G.M. sales", type="l")
lines(filter(Vendite, rep(1/3,3)), type="o", lty=2)
lines(filter(Vendite, rep(1/5,5)), type="l", lty=4, lwd=2)
```

