Now **R** will not include the December dummy. Suppose the model is exponential, so that logarithms are needed to linearise it

$$
\begin{gathered}Y=ab^{t}c_{1}^{D_{1}}c_{2}^{D_{2}}...c_{11}^{D_{11}}\to \\ \log Y=\log a+t\log b+D_{1}\log c_{1}+D_{2}\log c_{2}+...+D_{11}\log c_{11}\end{gathered}
\tag{4.12}
$$

So $(b-1)\cdot 100$ is the estimated compound monthly growth rate of our series $Y$, while the coefficients $c_{i}$ are the seasonal multipliers relative to December. We proceed with the estimation.

