  output out=fit_prod p=logfit;
run;
quit;
/* the antilogs of the estimates, exp(b), give the seasonal multipliers */
```
:::

Except for March, the seasonal effects are all statistically significant, but to recover the original coefficients we need the antilog. We find that product sales stood at 12.4 quintals at the start of the series (the intercept), with a compound monthly rate of change of 0.24% over the period considered. Specifically, in January, compared with December, sales fell on average by 9.39%. By contrast, November (again compared with December) shows an increase of about 18.24%.

